{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-415630-r4515259","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chocolate Chip Balls","sourcePageId":415630,"sourceRevision":"4515259","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T03:07:43Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chocolate%20Chip%20Balls&oldid=4515259","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:38:11.334Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for cookies","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using baking soda","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using dark chocolate","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using milk chocolate"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"bf3a4ec492125265d09cfc74945e9a1e6ac4c4f784e5d967b0a71ee8731455c2","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cookie recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThese '''chocolate chip balls''' are a baked good similar to chocolate chip cookies.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*2 sticks (1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]]) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], softened \n*1 cup (240 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) granulated white [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*1 cup (240 ml) packed [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n*2 extra-large [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]] \n*1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla Extract|vanilla extract]] \n*2 cups (480 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]]\n*2 cups (480 ml) [[Cookbook:Oat flour|oat flour]] \n*½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] \n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n*1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*2 cups (480 ml / 12 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) semi-sweet [[Cookbook:Chocolate|chocolate]] morsels or [[Cookbook:Chocolate chip|chocolate chips]]\n*4 oz (120 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]] / ½ bar) grated milk chocolate\n*3 cups (720 ml) chopped [[Cookbook:Nut|nuts]] (optional)\n\n==Procedure==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 375°F (around 200°C).\n#[[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] butter and both sugars in a large mixer bowl.  \n#[[Cookbook:Beating|Beat]] in eggs and vanilla extract.\n#[[Cookbook:Sifting|Sift]] together the flour, salt, oat flour, baking powder, and baking soda.  \n#Stir in chocolate morsels, grated chocolate bar, and nuts.\n#Roll into balls and place 2 [[Cookbook:Inch|inches]] apart on a [[Cookbook:Baking Sheet|cookie sheet]].\n#[[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 10 minutes or until golden brown (cooking times may vary). Remove and let stand for about 1 minute before moving cookies to a plate or [[Cookbook:Cooling Rack|cooling sheet]].\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Instead of a cookie sheet, you can also use a pizza stone.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using dark chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes for cookies]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk chocolate]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]","isRecipe":true,